From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 18:54:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] SECURITY-D2: removing a member clears their password

Sign-in refused a removed member's password only by reading the
allow-list, so adding the address back reopened the old password - known
to whoever learned it in the meantime - and the person re-adding them was
told only that they "can now sign in". Removal now deletes the
member_passwords row alongside revoking sessions and tokens; everything
else about the member is kept. Re-adding says the old password was
cleared, and the removal page says so before anybody confirms.

